                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 2 at 4:07AM CDT until September 2 at 5:00AM CDT by NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "description": "At 407 AM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 3 and 10 inches of rain have\nfallen. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLumberton, Silsbee, Woodville, Kountze, Sour Lake, Nome, Wildwood,\nWarren, Saratoga, Bevil Oaks, China, Village Mills, Honey Island,\nIvanhoe and Hillister.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFSLCH"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS74 KLCH 020907"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
                        "FLASH FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 5 AM CDT EARLY THIS MORNING FOR HARDIN, NORTHWESTERN JEFFERSON AND SOUTHWESTERN TYLER COUNTIES"
                    ],
